// 5.77 / A5 (increment 3): the distributed two-fluid row takes a STATIC
// WALL. Only the liquid share of each cell's wall can yield, so the drop
// the column can hold without moving is the distributed sum
//
//   dp_y = sum_i (4 dx_i / d) alpha_i tau_0,
//
// and the drive the wall has to resist is dp_drive - sum_i rho_m,i g sinT_i dx_i
// (zero gravity here, horizontal). At a uniform alpha this is exactly the
// single-phase 4 tau_0 L / d of 5.49 scaled by alpha: neither n nor K
// enters the threshold. The moving wall stress gains + alpha tau_0, so as
// u -> 0+ the laminar member tends to dp_y from ABOVE -- a sub-threshold
// drive would otherwise be answered by an equal REVERSE flow, the exact
// error 5.49 refused in the lumped row. Instead the held row is replaced
// by `u = 0`, latched once at the start of the step.
//
// THE ARM: pure liquid (alpha = 1 everywhere), horizontal, Wallis us = 0,
// L = 2, d = 0.02, N = 4 sections, muL = 0.1, tau_0 = 1 Pa, dp = 300 Pa.
//   dp_y = 4 * 1 * 2 / 0.02 = 400 Pa  >  dp = 300 Pa   -> HELD.
// Both ends are fixedPressure, so the momentum row is Newton-solved and
// the latch is the only thing that can hold it. The whole run must report
// vm = 0 with `static hold 1` on every sample after t = 0 (at t = 0 no
// step has been taken, so the constructor's 0 is reported).
//
// `dp` in the report is the FRICTION + GRAVITY loss the node-pressure march
// integrates, not the total drop: a held column reads no wall law, so it
// reports dp = 0 while the static wall silently supports all 300 Pa.
//
// siblings (same geometry/fluid, checker runs them itself):
//   case_open.dict    p 600  -> super-threshold; implicit-Euler recursion
//                              onto (p - dp_y) d^2 / (32 muL L) = 0.0125 m/s
//   case_graded.dict  fills make only the LAST HALF of the pipe liquid:
//                              dp_y = 200 Pa, so the SAME p 300 now opens.
//                              This is the distributed witness -- a
//                              geometry-only 400 Pa threshold would hold it.
//   case_newt.dict    yieldStress 0 -> zero declaration; the checker
//                              reproduces the 5.42 laminar start-up
//                              recursion frame by frame (bit-for-bit path)
//   case_cross.dict   initial vm 0.01 -> a MOVING column parks at u = 0 on
//                              the crossing witness, then the latch owns it
//   case_hb.dict      flowIndex 0.5 + consistency 0.1 + yieldStress 1:
//                              threshold is still 400 Pa (geometry only),
//                              the moving wall is Herschel-Bulkley
//   case_network.dict branch network: two spans, all branches held, the
//                              junction balance and the replaced rows coexist
// The checker also mutates this file in-place (under a probe name) for the
// band-edge p = 400, the graded band edges p = 199 / 201, a super-threshold
// network start-up that must RELEASE the latch, and the loud rejections.
fluid
{
    rhoL 1000;
    rhoG 20;
    muL  0.1;
    muG  1e-5;
    yieldStress 1;
}

pipe
{
    length 2;
    diameter 0.02;
    roughness 0;
    angleDeg 0;
    sections 4;
}

closure
{
    model wallis;
    slipVelocity 0;
}

initial
{
    alpha 1;
    water 0;
}

boundaries
{
    inlet  { type fixedPressure; p 300; alpha 1; waterFraction 0; }
    outlet { type fixedPressure; p 0; }
}

time
{
    dt 0.005;
    endTime 0.4;
    reportEvery 20;
}
